{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012rd58wD8AG49hQ9PZdhX6P","type":"tool_result","content":"<persisted-output>\nOutput too large (51.3KB). Full output saved to: /root/.claude/projects/-root-tank-simulation/6caedeb9-3152-4257-893d-1059836ae04b/tool-results/toolu_012rd58wD8AG49hQ9PZdhX6P.txt\n\nPreview (first 2KB):\n     1→\n     2→# Aquarium / Planted Tank Ecosystem Simulator — Implementation Spec (Rust)\n     3→\n     4→Version: 0.1  \n     5→Target system: freshwater planted shrimp tank (`Neocaridina davidi`)  \n     6→Primary UI: terminal / text UI  \n     7→Core requirement: scientifically grounded, deterministic, agent-implementable\n     8→\n     9→---\n    10→\n    11→## 1. Objective\n    12→\n    13→Build a Rust simulation engine that models a living freshwater planted aquarium as an ecosystem rather than a scripted set of events.\n    14→\n    15→The simulator must let a player:\n    16→\n    17→- configure tanks of different sizes and shapes\n    18→- stock and maintain a tank over time\n    19→- change husbandry variables, including **ambient temperature**\n    20→- observe chemistry, plant growth, algae, biofilm, microfauna, shrimp condition, and long-term stabilization\n    21→- encounter realistic emergent problems such as:\n    22→  - cycling delays\n    23→  - ammonia or nitrite stress\n    24→  - algae blooms\n    25→  - oxygen dips\n    26→  - breeding success/failure\n    27→  - molt issues\n    28→  - detritus accumulation\n    29→  - instability in small tanks compared with larger tanks\n    30→\n    31→The design must be specific enough that an implementation agent can build the system incrementally without re-architecting the codebase.\n    32→\n    33→---\n    34→\n    35→## 2. Scope\n    36→\n    37→## 2.1 In scope for v1\n    38→\n    39→A single freshwater tank containing:\n    40→\n    41→- water column\n    42→- tank geometry and water volume\n    43→- substrate\n    44→- filter / biomedia compartment\n    45→- heater (optional but supported)\n    46→- light\n    47→- rooted plants\n    48→- periphyton / biofilm\n    49→- free algae\n    50→- microbial guilds\n    51→- microfauna guilds\n    52→- shrimp population\n    53→- detritus / dissolved organics\n    54→- player maintenance actions\n    55→\n    56→## 2.2 Out of scope for v1\n    57→\n    58→- photorealistic graphics\n...\n</persisted-output>"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01NTJRfgX9Yf8u1ahRrw9C8p","session_id":"6caedeb9-3152-4257-893d-1059836ae04b","uuid":"ffff4291-1cb7-4f45-827b-6735eca53990"}
